{
  "case_id": "2008-07-665",
  "document_hash": "cc18b9aac33c234b973dedf4d41831ac061fa7c88b31993932229295c27e88b1",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-07-665",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cc18b9aac33c234b973dedf4d41831ac061fa7c88b31993932229295c27e88b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cc18b9aac33c-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:13 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2008-07-665",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cc18b9aac33c234b973dedf4d41831ac061fa7c88b31993932229295c27e88b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cc18b9aac33c-0000-0001",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "DARYL JOSEFFER, ESQ., Deputy Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the United States, as amicus curiae, supporting the Petitioners."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2008-07-665",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cc18b9aac33c234b973dedf4d41831ac061fa7c88b31993932229295c27e88b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cc18b9aac33c-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Tenth Circuit erred when it held that the First Amendment Free Speech Clause forces Pleasant Grove City to accept and erect on its property a private party's donated, unattended, permanent monument."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2008-07-665",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cc18b9aac33c234b973dedf4d41831ac061fa7c88b31993932229295c27e88b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cc18b9aac33c-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: Mr. Sekulow, can I just ask: At what point in the litigation did you first raise the Government speech argument?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2008-07-665",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cc18b9aac33c234b973dedf4d41831ac061fa7c88b31993932229295c27e88b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cc18b9aac33c-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "they are controlling on the basis of agreement with the message. Why isn't that a First Amendment violation?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2008-07-665",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cc18b9aac33c234b973dedf4d41831ac061fa7c88b31993932229295c27e88b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cc18b9aac33c-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I don't think that can you avoid the hard part by saying, oh, other amendments of the Constitution might apply. The heart of the question is whether the Government may discriminate based on content, and that's a First Amendment question."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2008-07-665",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cc18b9aac33c234b973dedf4d41831ac061fa7c88b31993932229295c27e88b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cc18b9aac33c-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So this case -- your claim would disappear if this town in Utah had passed an ordinance saying we adopt the Ten Commandments Monument?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "City of Pleasant Grove",
      "case_id": "2008-07-665",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cc18b9aac33c234b973dedf4d41831ac061fa7c88b31993932229295c27e88b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cc18b9aac33c-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The only way the Government can be adopting anything in this context is by saying through the act of selection we have adopted it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-07-665",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cc18b9aac33c234b973dedf4d41831ac061fa7c88b31993932229295c27e88b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cc18b9aac33c-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is there an historical basis for that, or you just made it up?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2008-07-665",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cc18b9aac33c234b973dedf4d41831ac061fa7c88b31993932229295c27e88b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cc18b9aac33c-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Isn't merely allowing the monument to be built on public property sufficient acceptance?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-07-665",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cc18b9aac33c234b973dedf4d41831ac061fa7c88b31993932229295c27e88b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cc18b9aac33c-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Would that be enough?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Harris",
      "case_id": "2008-07-665",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cc18b9aac33c234b973dedf4d41831ac061fa7c88b31993932229295c27e88b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cc18b9aac33c-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the Government speech here is only in the act of selection. Selection. It's not about the content of that monument. That's not enough to make a Government speech, and the City is not permitted to speak through selection, and --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2008-07-665",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cc18b9aac33c234b973dedf4d41831ac061fa7c88b31993932229295c27e88b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cc18b9aac33c-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 61,
        "start": 61
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Give one and I'll read it. Give me three; I'll read them."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Harris",
      "case_id": "2008-07-665",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cc18b9aac33c234b973dedf4d41831ac061fa7c88b31993932229295c27e88b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cc18b9aac33c-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 61,
        "start": 61
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I'll give you Pinette. The Government can't make content based decisions in a public forum."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2008-07-665",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "cc18b9aac33c234b973dedf4d41831ac061fa7c88b31993932229295c27e88b1",
